\paragraph{Pathwise.}
Because the state is continuous, the reparameterisation is already written in~\eqref{eq:chain}: $y_k$ is a deterministic function of $\theta$ given the noise. If a critic $V_\phi(y_k,t_k,c)$ estimates the expected reward of a noisy state, then
\begin{equation}
\hat g_{\mathrm{PW}}=\frac{\partial V_\phi(y_k)}{\partial y_k}\;\alpha_k\,\frac{\partial D_\theta(y_{k-1})}{\partial\theta}
\label{eq:pw}
\end{equation}
delivers a deterministic, per-coordinate signal whose magnitude is set by the critic's local slope rather than by $\varepsilon_k/\sigma_k$. This is the estimator of continuous control \citep{lillicrap2015ddpg,haarnoja2018sac} and of reward back-propagation through image diffusion \citep{prabhudesai2023alignprop,clark2023draft,domingoenrich2024adjoint}. It is absent from AR post-training for one reason: categorical sampling has no reparameterisation, and its relaxations \citep{jang2016gumbel,maddison2016concrete} are biased. Its known failure mode is equally specific: the policy climbs the critic rather than the reward unless the critic tracks the policy. Section~\ref{sec:method} builds the critic that makes~\eqref{eq:pw} work, and \S\ref{sec:ablations} shows that freezing it removes the gains.
